# Uforge

Read `doc/vision.md` first, then `doc/architecture.md`. The vision page wins over any other doc, code comment or habit. The code was rebuilt on this vision on 2026-10-18; what is done, tested and still missing is in "État du code" / "Reste à faire" of `doc/architecture.md`. Keep docs and code in sync when you change either.

Product in one line: an empty app that becomes any JS app through an AI conversation. The admin's Uforge password protects the workshop and encrypts what comes out of it. "Builder" validates the app; it can then be exported/imported as a `.happ` file.

Non-negotiables:
- The generation AI writes real code (project files) through the `uf-*` protocol. Never reintroduce a fixed spec, page types or a template catalogue.
- One app per Runtime install. No app manager.
- The device is the source of truth for the app. The gateway never stores source, builds, `.happ` files or app data.
- Never persist the admin password (no localStorage, sessionStorage or disk).
- Generated apps run only in the sandboxed iframe and reach the device only through `runtime.*`. Nothing in `runtime.*` can open the workshop or read the admin block.
- No AI provider calls from `services/web`: all generation goes through `services/gateway`.
- `skills/prompt/` frames the generation AI; `doc/` frames developers. Keep `skills/prompt/30-runtime-api.md` identical to `doc/features/device-bridge.md`, and `skills/prompt/10-output-protocol.md` in sync with the gateway parser.

Pages: features in `doc/features/<name>.md`, technos in `doc/techno/<name>.md`.

JSDoc and code comments in English with an `@example`. Product `doc/` is in French.

Stack: Docker Compose, NestJS gateway, Prisma/Postgres, Redis, esbuild compiler, Vue 3 + Vite Runtime, Capacitor Android.
